     ∇ Z←T SEQTWO V;N;R ⍝ RETROAPL V4.6
[1]  ⍝ TWO VOICES IN THE OLD NOTE-FILE LAYOUT TO TWO SEQUENCER TRACKS.
[2]  ⍝ V: N, THEN N PITCHES FOR VOICE 1, N FOR VOICE 2, N SHARED DURATIONS
[3]  ⍝ (RESTS FAKED BY LENGTHENING THE PREVIOUS NOTE, AS THE FILE HAS THEM).
[4]  ⍝ T: THE TWO TRACK NUMBERS. Z: THE BEATS AT WHICH EACH TAKES OVER.
[5]  N←V[⎕IO]
[6]  R←1↓V
[7]  Z←((1↑T) ⎕SEQTRACK (2,N)⍴(N↑R),(2×N)↓R),(1↓T) ⎕SEQTRACK (2,N)⍴(N↑N↓R),(2×N)↓R
